# Clean code habits

Day-to-day readability. See also `frontend-solid` and `frontend-fp` for design principles.

## Habits

- **DRY (carefully):** Extract repeated logic only when the same rule appears in multiple places and would change together — not for one-off similarity.
- Prefer early returns over deep `if` nesting.
- Name things after domain intent (`timeRange`, `fetchBtcPriceHistory`), not vague helpers (`data`, `handleStuff`).
- Avoid drive-by refactors — change only what the task needs.
- Comments explain non-obvious why; do not narrate what the next line does.
- Delete dead code and unused exports instead of leaving them “for later”.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — nested control flow, vague names, narrating comment
function Panel(props: any) {
  if (props.data) {
    if (props.data.items) {
      // map the items
      return props.data.items.map((x: any) => <div>{x.t}</div>)
    }
  }
  return null
}

// ✅ GOOD — early return, clear names
function AlertTitleList({ titles }: { titles: string[] }) {
  if (titles.length === 0) return null
  return titles.map((title) => <div key={title}>{title}</div>)
}
```
